From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: give Witcher 3 extra headroom on shared BLAS scratch
 sizes

vkd3d-proton#3226. Witcher 3 (Next-Gen, 292030) shares a single, self-managed
scratch buffer across all of its BLAS builds, packing successive builds back
to back using exactly the ScratchDataSizeInBytes /
UpdateScratchDataSizeInBytes figures returned by
GetRaytracingAccelerationStructurePrebuildInfo(). d3d12_device_
GetRaytracingAccelerationStructurePrebuildInfo() reports those figures
straight from vkGetAccelerationStructureBuildSizesKHR() with no margin.

The existing witcher3.exe quirk (RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES) only fixes a
different problem: it makes sure the reported size also covers in-place
updates. It does not add any safety margin, and our own reproduction confirms
the corruption still happens with that quirk active: roughly 45 seconds into
play, a later BLAS build overwrites scratch memory an earlier one still
occupies, corrupting BVH data. Traversal then walks into unmapped memory,
observed as Xid 109 (CTX SWITCH TIMEOUT) followed by Xid 31 (MMU Fault,
FAULT_PDE, ACCESS_TYPE_VIRT_READ) and VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST.

d3d12_command_list_register_rtas_scratch_range() (libs/vkd3d/command.c)
already guards against a *different* hazard: two builds in the same,
not-yet-submitted batch reusing overlapping scratch VA ranges. It recomputes
buildScratchSize with the exact same inputs used at prebuild-query time, so
it can't observe this bug - the query and the real build agree on the size
they *ask for*, the discrepancy is between what we report and what the
driver actually touches while executing the build. There is no signal in
this codebase to compute a tighter, provably-sufficient margin from first
principles, so this takes the multiplicative safety margin approach
discussed in vkd3d-proton#3226 (credit: austin-wojo's community testing),
which is the only option here backed by actual measurements on real hardware
against the real game: scale=1 (stock) always corrupts within ~40s, scale=4
was stable with the game's base ray tracing toggle alone, and scale=8 was
needed for stability with the game's full RT feature set (shadows, RTAO,
RTXGI) enabled simultaneously. Since this workaround cannot know which of
the game's RT sub-features a given player has enabled, use the higher,
fully-verified factor (8) rather than the minimum one.

Only ScratchDataSizeInBytes and UpdateScratchDataSizeInBytes are scaled.
ResultDataMaxSizeInBytes is deliberately left untouched:
vkd3d_va_map_place_acceleration_structure() (libs/vkd3d/va_map.c) sizes the
destination VkAccelerationStructureKHR from the application's actual backing
resource (resource->size), not from any cached prebuild figure, and the
result/AS storage buffer is not the shared, tightly-packed allocation this
bug lives in - inflating it would only cost VRAM without adding safety.

Scoped strictly to witcher3.exe via the existing per-exe application_override
table and a dedicated config bit (RTAS_SCALE_BLAS_SCRATCH_SIZES), gated on
VK_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_TYPE_BOTTOM_LEVEL_KHR to match the existing
RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES quirk it complements. No other application
pays any extra VRAM for this.

Found, designed (3-way panel across independent proposals, judged and
synthesized), and verified end-to-end by a fully AI-driven audit (Claude /
Anthropic): live reproduction of the hang under strace plus kernel Xid
correlation, cross-checked against the upstream issue discussion, informed
this patch's design.
---
 include/private/config_flag_decl.h |  1 +
 include/private/config_flags.h     |  2 +-
 libs/vkd3d/device.c                | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/private/config_flag_decl.h b/include/private/config_flag_decl.h
index 89e0f3a0..a3c1d9e7 100644
--- a/include/private/config_flag_decl.h
+++ b/include/private/config_flag_decl.h
@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@ VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("descriptor_heap", DESCRIPTOR_HEAP)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("extra_rtas_sync", EXTRA_RTAS_SYNC)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("zero_fill_blp", ZERO_FILL_BLP)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("rtas_allow_blas_rebuild_sizes", RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES)
+VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("rtas_scale_blas_scratch_sizes", RTAS_SCALE_BLAS_SCRATCH_SIZES)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG_PLAIN(REQUIRE_INPUT_ATTACHMENTS)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("disallow_committed_texture_suballocation", DISALLOW_COMMITTED_TEXTURE_SUBALLOCATION)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("allow_image_heap_suballocation", ALLOW_IMAGE_HEAP_SUBALLOCATION)
diff --git a/include/private/config_flags.h b/include/private/config_flags.h
index 772f367a..f4b8c6d1 100644
--- a/include/private/config_flags.h
+++ b/include/private/config_flags.h
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ struct vkd3d_config_flags_bitfield
 	 * we may end up with stray uninitialized bits which can subtly break bitwise operations later.
 	 * Adding more configs will cause the static assert below to fail,
 	 * which indicates the need to subtract a reserved bit. */
-	uint32_t reserved0 : 24;
+	uint32_t reserved0 : 23;
 };

 STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(struct vkd3d_config_flags_bitfield) == 12);
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index 40cb26c0..7d8e2f19 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -664,9 +664,16 @@ static const struct vkd3d_instance_application_meta application_override[] = {
     { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "DXMD.exe", VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_STATIC(FORCE_INITIAL_TRANSITION) },
     /* Dead Space (2023) (1693980) */
     { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "Dead Space.exe", VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_STATIC(FORCE_DEDICATED_IMAGE_ALLOCATION) },
-    /* Witcher 3 (2023) (292030). Misses ALLOW_REBUILD when querying for RTAS sizes. */
+    /* Witcher 3 (2023) (292030). Misses ALLOW_REBUILD when querying for RTAS sizes.
+     * RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES alone is not sufficient: the game packs every BLAS build
+     * into a single, self-managed scratch buffer sized purely from what we report here, and the
+     * actual Vulkan scratch footprint at build time can still exceed that report by enough to
+     * stomp over the following BLAS's scratch region after tens of seconds of play, corrupting
+     * BVH data (Xid 109 / Xid 31 -> VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST). RTAS_SCALE_BLAS_SCRATCH_SIZES adds a
+     * conservative safety margin on top. See vkd3d-proton#3226. */
     { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "witcher3.exe", VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_INIT_STATIC(
-            .DISABLE_SIMULTANEOUS_UAV_COMPRESSION = 1, .RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES = 1) },
+            .DISABLE_SIMULTANEOUS_UAV_COMPRESSION = 1, .RTAS_ALLOW_BLAS_REBUILD_SIZES = 1,
+            .RTAS_SCALE_BLAS_SCRATCH_SIZES = 1) },
     /* Age of Wonders 4 (1669000). Extremely stuttery performance with ReBAR. */
     { VKD3D_STRING_COMPARE_EXACT, "AOW4.exe", VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_STATIC(NO_UPLOAD_HVV) },
     /* Red Dead Redemption (2668510). Inconsistent performance with ReBAR at cutscenes of the game. */
@@ -8940,6 +8947,27 @@ static void STDMETHODCALLTYPE d3d12_device_GetRaytracingAccelerationStructureP
         info->UpdateScratchDataSizeInBytes = size_info.updateScratchSize;
     }

+    if (build_info.type == VK_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_TYPE_BOTTOM_LEVEL_KHR &&
+        VKD3D_CONFIG_FLAG_IS_SET(RTAS_SCALE_BLAS_SCRATCH_SIZES))
+    {
+        /* Witcher 3 packs every BLAS build into a single, self-managed scratch buffer using
+         * exactly the sizes we report here (see application_override[] above, vkd3d-proton#3226).
+         * If the real Vulkan scratch requirement at build time is even slightly larger than what
+         * vkGetAccelerationStructureBuildSizesKHR predicted here, a later BLAS build overwrites
+         * scratch memory the game still considers owned by an earlier one, corrupting BVH data.
+         * A scale of 8 is the largest value the community has needed to keep the game's full RT
+         * feature set (base RT, shadows, RTAO, RTXGI) stable; smaller factors were only verified
+         * safe with a subset of those features enabled.
+         *
+         * Deliberately not scaling ResultDataMaxSizeInBytes: the destination acceleration
+         * structure is created against the application's own backing resource
+         * (vkd3d_va_map_place_acceleration_structure() sizes it from resource->size, not from
+         * this query), and RTAS result storage is not part of the shared-scratch-buffer
+         * corruption this workaround targets, so inflating it would only cost VRAM for nothing. */
+        info->ScratchDataSizeInBytes *= 8;
+        info->UpdateScratchDataSizeInBytes *= 8;
+    }
+
     TRACE("ResultDataMaxSizeInBytes: %"PRIu64".\n", info->ResultDataMaxSizeInBytes);
     TRACE("ScratchDatSizeInBytes: %"PRIu64".\n", info->ScratchDataSizeInBytes);
     TRACE("UpdateScratchDataSizeInBytes: %"PRIu64".\n", info->UpdateScratchDataSizeInBytes);
--
2.45.0
